  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Satendra Singh Tomar vs The State Of Madhya Pradesh on 7 April, 2021 Author: Sheel Nagu Bench: Sheel Nagu 1 Mcrc-16354-2021 The High Court Of Madhya Pradesh Mcrc-16354-2021 (Satendra Singh Tomar Vs. State of M.P.)",
    "facts": "This is second bail application u/S.439 CrPC filed by the petitioner for grant of bail after rejection of earlier one which was dismissed on 15.03.2021 in M.Cr.C. No.10685/2021 with liberty to the petitioner to revisit this Court after conclusion of investigation. The petitioner has been arrested on 30.01.2021 by Police Station - Sihoniya, District Morena (M.P.), in connection with Crime No. 19/2021 registered in relation to the offences punishable u/s.420, 272, 273 of IPC and Section 51, 57, 58 and 59 of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006. Petitioner, who is in custody since 30.01.2021, is alleged with aforementioned offences. Earlier one was dismissed with liberty to the petitioner to revisit this court after conclusion of investigation. New ground raised is that investigation in the matter is over by 2 MCRC-16354-2021 filing of charge-sheet on 17.03.2021.",
    "arguments": "Learned counsel for State opposed the application and prayed for its rejection by contending that on the basis of the allegations and the material available on record, no case for grant of bail is made out.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "Learned counsel for State opposed the application and prayed for its rejection by contending that on the basis of the allegations and the material available on record, no case for grant of bail is made out.",
